[00:10.06] Are you goin' to Scarborough Fair?
[00:16.79] Parsley, sage, rosemary and thyme
[00:23.11] 
[00:25.27] Remember me to one who lives there
[00:32.25] She once was a true love of mine
[00:41.64] 
[00:44.18] Tell her to make me a cambric shirt
[00:48.44] (On the side of a hill in the deep forest green)
[00:51.22] Parsley, sage, rosemary and thyme
[00:54.82] (Tracing a sparrow on snow-crested ground)
[00:59.08] Without no seams nor needlework
[01:03.97] (Blankets and bedclothes, the child of the mountain)
[01:07.05] Then she'll be a true love of mine
[01:11.56] (Sleeps unaware of a clarion call)
[01:16.45] Tell her to find me an acre of land
[01:20.04] (On the side of a hill, a sprinkling of leaves)
[01:23.30] Parsley, sage, rosemary and thyme
[01:27.46] (Washes the grave with silvery tears)
[01:31.61] Between the salt water and the sea strand
[01:37.67] (A soldier cleans and polishes a gun)
[01:40.53] Then she'll be a true love of mine
[01:45.93] 
[01:49.68] Tell her to reap it in a sickle of leather
[01:53.81] (War bellows blazing in scarlet battalions)
[01:56.94] Parsley, sage, rosemary and thyme
[02:00.72] (Generals order their soldiers to kill)
[02:05.51] And gather it all in a bunch of heather
[02:10.66] (And to fight for a cause they've long ago forgotten)
[02:13.66] Then she'll be a true love of mine
[02:19.38] 
[02:23.75] Are you goin' to Scarborough Fair?
[02:29.66] 
[02:32.01] Parsley, sage, rosemary and thyme
[02:38.77] Remember me to one who lives there
